In article <3834@blake.acs.washington.edu> nickel@blake.acs.washington.edu (Robert DeLoura) writes:
>In article <14838@netnews.upenn.edu> song@grad1.cis.upenn.edu.UUCP (Mitchell So
>ng) writes:
>:I would like to make a request for a monk character in nethack.
>:He would gain special skills as his level increases with the altimate skill
>:being the finger of death.  Also, his best weapon would be his hand. 
>:As he increases in level, he would do increasingly more damage with his
>:hand.
>
>The Samurai is sort of like this already, except he kicks instead of using
>his hands.  But if this *were* to be implemented, something would need to
>be done to counterbalance the fact that he can't possibly have his weapon
>rusted, damaged by a scroll, lost, cursed, etc.  

As a low level character, it would actually be a disadvantage to use just
his hands, since bare hands do very little damage.  He/She would still
need to carry some sort of weapon to counter the cockatrice and maybe some
others. Also, I wouldn't call NOT being able to use swords like Excalibur
or Snickersnee an advantage.  He should, however, be able to use the 
axe type artifacts (which aren't as powerful). 

The only time a charater has problems with cursed weapons is early in the
game when he/she is looking for a good weapon (I've never had any problems
once I found the desired weapon). The Monk is subject to this also as he/she
needs to find a good weapon to use early on. 
Besides, getting rid of cursed weapons isn't that difficult.

As for rusting, anyone can easily make there weapon rust proof. They can
also enchant their weapons to have pluses. Since Monks use their hands,
they don't get this benefit. As for damage by scrolls, this would happen
only once during a game (unless someone wants to do this intentionally).

>Perhaps he can be restricted
>to wearing no full-body armor whatsoever.  After all, Monks in AD&D, which
>you quote as your source, can't do it either.  That would take this potential
>new character class down a step or two, I'd say.  :)
>

If I remember correctly, armor class of Monks go down as they increase in
level.  It may be a hard character to play early on compared to others, 
but this would change as the character gained experience, if he survives 
that long.


